peratorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, the formula above and the chain rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{arccot} {x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} {x}^{3})+\\operatorname{arccot} {x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{1+{({x}^{3})}^{2}}\\right)+\\operatorname{arccot} {x}^{3}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} {x}^{3}}{x}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08847216-8695-5c58-9c55-4efd9ea37cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284855} {:answer/id #uuid "713ca5fb-8006-5933-96ce-17ac96219558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285826} {:answer/id #uuid "75c3ab8f-18e2-59e5-b409-f23279f422cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{({x}^{3}+2x)(3{x}^{2}+2)}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285882} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bb6a0e-a3e1-53de-bf1c-a588c28c1165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286254} {:answer/id #uuid "a3628ab9-5c34-5c92-bef6-1314d9e06e81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08847216-8695-5c58-9c55-4efd9ea37cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284855} :answer-field/id #uuid "751d5f7c-e24c-5495-bd5f-426fdee41841" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd1d008a-84eb-52df-bb09-d41421bc5f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-19065" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=({x}^{3}+2x)\\operatorname{arccot} x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(({x}^{3}+2x)\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+2x)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+2)+({x}^{3}+2x)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{arccot} x-\\frac{{x}^{3}+2x}{{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290578 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3e8a72-d66c-5ec3-b40f-fb6c49116d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288134} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc58f79-67c9-5a07-82b8-37019e8fcf16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288210} {:answer/id #uuid "356f78a7-7f7f-5f9a-acab-fbad74f70904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288391} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9cda91-25c7-507c-ae14-575d705818bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} x}{x(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288670} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd2ac71-6b4c-5d57-94e6-568eed9deb7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bc58f79-67c9-5a07-82b8-37019e8fcf16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288210} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ae30e1-e24b-51c6-ac9f-1b57607c624a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289785}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0452209a-6bf5-5ff9-86d8-fd513bd202d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-2483" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccot} x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111f643e-21fe-5850-a34c-7e75f866dffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288160} {:answer/id #uuid "5476c042-8711-54ab-b3d4-eadca3ea72e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288614} {:answer/id #uuid "6427fa83-3424-5638-881a-1b75c59158ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288737} {:answer/id #uuid "8d34a562-2280-5df3-b021-0fc8376c8ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x-\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288975} {:answer/id #uuid "f32241a6-5d82-568c-bcfd-3f92960cb105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x+\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d34a562-2280-5df3-b021-0fc8376c8ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x-\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288975} :answer-field/id #uuid "352c605b-c2ce-576c-94c4-6d4a6fa3df72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fabb0dc5-fadf-5950-bf52-26606893c541" :question/math-academy-id "q-2484" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsec} x$" :question/worked-solution "The formulae for the derivatives of $\\operatorname{arccsc} $ and $\\operatorname{arcsec} $ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x) & =-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{arcsec} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccsc} x)+\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsec} x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsec} x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right)+\\operatorname{arccsc} x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc} x-\\operatorname{arcsec} x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315055 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2d52500-a992-5060-8249-a0e5114ed838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2d52500-a992-5060-8249-a0e5114ed838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313765} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e24a99-cc76-5643-98c9-e83dbb7d91d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0bdae838-0b95-584e-856d-e0740682daed" :question/math-academy-id "q-341145" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,(\\sqrt{x}).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{1+x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} (\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0c4566c-bd79-5868-a603-18f0216abcb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0c4566c-bd79-5868-a603-18f0216abcb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313607} :answer-field/id #uuid "183d9fe6-f1f2-5fd2-b79e-60dbadd9be0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314073}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c596781e-b79d-5304-abff-1db8b7bfbe7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341146" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08831fa4-e925-511e-9c83-0ad4ccc9d162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{4}x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08831fa4-e925-511e-9c83-0ad4ccc9d162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{4}x}{1+{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312036} :answer-field/id #uuid "b52cc14c-ea3a-52a9-8673-3631dde0a4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314499}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88e0b1bd-ab5b-5056-934f-dc0524e7e997" :question/math-academy-id "q-341147" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={\\log }_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot} $ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\log }_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\log }_{4}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{\\log }_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot \\operatorname{arccot} \\,x+{\\log }_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot} \\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{{\\log }_{4}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Inverse cotangent has derivative $-1/(1+x^2)$; the square-root denominator belongs to a different inverse trigonometric derivative." :answer/id #uuid "2501708a-8ba2-5378-81ba-655f3539bce8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746686} {:answer/feedback "The derivative of a product is the sum of two products, not the product of the derivatives." :answer/id #uuid "6616d854-4a8b-555d-82ad-f291eb56891d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746693} {:answer/feedback "The factor $x$ remains unchanged in the term containing the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot}(x)$." :answer/id #uuid "7d3f3663-157e-5036-bb02-dd2e6216dc26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746695} {:answer/feedback "Correct. Each term differentiates one factor and leaves the other unchanged." :answer/id #uuid "8974a753-ff75-5d46-96f6-3069fe8aef43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{x}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746699} {:answer/feedback "The derivative of $\\operatorname{arccot}(x)$ is negative." :answer/id #uuid "df2a7c7e-f7e6-5bff-b525-fef3abf2a1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot}(x)+\\frac{x}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. Each term differentiates one factor and leaves the other unchanged." :answer/id #uuid "8974a753-ff75-5d46-96f6-3069fe8aef43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{x}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746699} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2fa1563-56e6-5e2c-ae45-064254ef9cb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746701}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0c88b167-0cd3-5c68-a680-1c455ee2a07c" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=x\\operatorname{arccot}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "The derivative of inverse cotangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccot}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the product, leaving one factor unchanged in each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=1\\cdot\\operatorname{arccot}(x)+x\\left(-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{x}{1+x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two derivatives would omit the unchanged factors and would not apply the product rule."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "The factor $\\ln(x)$ remains unchanged in the term that differentiates inverse secant." :answer/id #uuid "25cf3a7d-5e2e-528e-a89d-8bf7013847ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746687} {:answer/feedback "The squared argument in the radical is $(x^2)^2=x^4$, not $x^2$." :answer/id #uuid "4e34ff81-43bc-50c7-a997-20bda01e7de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}+\\frac{2\\ln(x)}{x\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746691} {:answer/feedback "Correct. The product rule retains both factors and the chain rule supplies the derivative of the inner square." :answer/id #uuid "7f9a0e10-cbd9-5563-8a1c-46a4baa72bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}+\\frac{2\\ln(x)}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746696} {:answer/feedback "The inverse secant derivative must be multiplied by the inner derivative $2x$." :answer/id #uuid "8613e218-505f-5b95-b446-02a52bcb2268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}+\\frac{\\ln(x)}{x^2\\sqrt{x^4-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746697} {:answer/feedback "The inverse secant derivative is positive on this domain; inverse cosecant has the negative formula." :answer/id #uuid "be03889a-39ad-5355-9df9-a08384f60468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}-\\frac{2\\ln(x)}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. The product rule retains both factors and the chain rule supplies the derivative of the inner square." :answer/id #uuid "7f9a0e10-cbd9-5563-8a1c-46a4baa72bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}+\\frac{2\\ln(x)}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746696} :answer-field/id #uuid "6954b50a-ca88-5a25-872d-aef7eed9209c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746694}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "51c48b2d-4966-5c56-a87a-805df496382c" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\ln(x)\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)$." :question/worked-solution "The inverse secant derivative and chain rule give\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arcsec}(u(x))=\n\\frac{u'(x)}{|u(x)|\\sqrt{u(x)^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nHere $u(x)=x^2$ and $u'(x)=2x$. The real domain of the product is $x\\geq1$, and we differentiate on $x>1$. Thus $|x^2|=x^2$, and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)\n&=\\frac{2x}{x^2\\sqrt{x^4-1}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow apply the product rule, using $(\\ln x)'=1/x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{1}{x}\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)\n +\\ln(x)\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x^2)}{x}\n +\\frac{2\\ln(x)}{x\\sqrt{x^4-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain factor $2x$ differentiates the argument $x^2$; it does not replace that argument inside inverse secant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Multiplying the two derivatives does not give the derivative of the product." :answer/id #uuid "02614c01-d1c7-5871-8920-c9cb01d3f699" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746683} {:answer/feedback "The inverse cosecant derivative carries a minus sign." :answer/id #uuid "2e6269c3-944d-5982-81a9-033a43566ac1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)+\\frac{x^2+1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746688} {:answer/feedback "The term that differentiates inverse cosecant must retain the whole factor $x^2+1$." :answer/id #uuid "42528589-ee25-50c4-9603-778597009dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746689} {:answer/feedback "Correct. Both product-rule terms and the absolute value are retained." :answer/id #uuid "4de10486-0dbb-59ee-91f3-3f286c7f195b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)-\\frac{x^2+1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746690} {:answer/feedback "The denominator needs $|x|$. Replacing it by $x$ changes the derivative when $x<-1$." :answer/id #uuid "d65b0a55-5609-5c1b-9fb2-4bf065d70792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)-\\frac{x^2+1}{x\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Correct. Both product-rule terms and the absolute value are retained." :answer/id #uuid "4de10486-0dbb-59ee-91f3-3f286c7f195b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)-\\frac{x^2+1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746690} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d018c76-24f2-5a29-ad3a-d8e4994b4608" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746685}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "887af645-be87-5b28-aa7b-5f4a1c1fdf16" :question/problem "Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=(x^2+1)\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)$." :question/worked-solution "For $|x|>1$, the derivative of inverse cosecant is\n\n$$\n\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n$$\n\nApply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2+1)\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)\n +(x^2+1)\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)\\\\\n&=2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)\n +(x^2+1)\\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\\\\\n&=2x\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)-\\frac{x^2+1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value must remain: the function is defined for negative as well as positive inputs with $|x|>1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6948d45e-5010-59e2-9c97-16bb52dfe387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)}{x\\ln(4)}-\\frac{\\log_{4}(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6948d45e-5010-59e2-9c97-16bb52dfe387" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)}{x\\ln(4)}-\\frac{\\log_{4}(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746768} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc841dd-b6fd-5c08-a10a-96dbb0164dfd" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746769}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "570e562f-824b-53e4-8b3d-c995a298acbb" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\left(\\log_{4}(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)\\right)$.\n\n{{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Work on the interior of the real domain: $x>0$, with $|x|>1$. For the inverse factor, the derivative formula gives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Here the argument and its derivative are $u(x)=x$ and $u'(x)=1$.\n\nSet $p(x)=\\log_{4}(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)$. Then $p'(x)=\\frac{1}{x\\ln(4)}$ and $v'(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=p'(x)v(x)+p(x)v'(x)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\ln(4)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(\\log_{4}(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMove each unchanged factor into its fraction numerator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccsc}(x)}{x\\ln(4)}\\\\\n&\\quad -\\frac{\\log_{4}(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6397c6-b49a-51f7-a6df-b40e40ddcf6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)}{x}+\\frac{\\ln(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c6397c6-b49a-51f7-a6df-b40e40ddcf6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)}{x}+\\frac{\\ln(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746764} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba2292e-9590-522d-9ca2-c9207ffc8c65" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746771}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "770e3854-22c8-5264-84d7-699b8e7aa46c" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\left(\\ln(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)\\right)$.\n\n{{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Work on the interior of the real domain: $x>0$, with $|x|>1$. For the inverse factor, the derivative formula gives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Here the argument and its derivative are $u(x)=x$ and $u'(x)=1$.\n\nSet $p(x)=\\ln(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)$. Then $p'(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $v'(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=p'(x)v(x)+p(x)v'(x)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(\\ln(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMove each unchanged factor into its fraction numerator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)}{x}\\\\\n&\\quad +\\frac{\\ln(x)}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a019d957-ebbf-5164-afee-567a133590a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x\\,\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{-2x^{2}-2}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a019d957-ebbf-5164-afee-567a133590a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4x\\,\\operatorname{arccot}(x)-\\frac{-2x^{2}-2}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746774} :answer-field/id #uuid "989e8e32-668b-5a5e-b2af-cfa35498edd0" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746773}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ee73227-5205-5bc3-be96-94864f399389" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\left(-2x^{2}-2\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccot}(x)\\right)$.\n\n{{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Work on the interior of the real domain: all real inputs. For the inverse factor, the derivative formula gives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccot}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$. Here the argument and its derivative are $u(x)=x$ and $u'(x)=1$.\n\nSet $p(x)=-2x^{2}-2$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arccot}(x)$. Then $p'(x)=-4x$ and $v'(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$. Apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=p'(x)v(x)+p(x)v'(x)\\\\\n&=\\left(-4x\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccot}(x)\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(-2x^{2}-2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMove each unchanged factor into its fraction numerator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=-4x\\,\\operatorname{arccot}(x)\\\\\n&\\quad -\\frac{-2x^{2}-2}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb1f7e93-bd6e-5067-9ed2-a79c4ed5275d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot}(x)}{x\\ln(7)}-\\frac{\\log_{7}(x)}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb1f7e93-bd6e-5067-9ed2-a79c4ed5275d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot}(x)}{x\\ln(7)}-\\frac{\\log_{7}(x)}{1+x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746778} :answer-field/id #uuid "e55cd43b-d324-50e2-9af2-67a33337e4fa" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746776}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0567c3f-e1a2-5704-8f4e-7b097f88b96e" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\left(\\log_{7}(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccot}(x)\\right)$.\n\n{{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Work on the interior of the real domain: $x>0$. For the inverse factor, the derivative formula gives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arccot}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$. Here the argument and its derivative are $u(x)=x$ and $u'(x)=1$.\n\nSet $p(x)=\\log_{7}(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arccot}(x)$. Then $p'(x)=\\frac{1}{x\\ln(7)}$ and $v'(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}$. Apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=p'(x)v(x)+p(x)v'(x)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{x\\ln(7)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arccot}(x)\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(\\log_{7}(x)\\right)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{1+x^2}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMove each unchanged factor into its fraction numerator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccot}(x)}{x\\ln(7)}\\\\\n&\\quad -\\frac{\\log_{7}(x)}{1+x^2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186746777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ba067ac-b662-5dc7-a26f-a44346c5da9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)+\\frac{e^{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba067ac-b662-5dc7-a26f-a44346c5da9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)+\\frac{e^{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746765} :answer-field/id #uuid "61380768-9016-5c00-a7d9-2e0061241879" :answer-field/key "derivative" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186746767}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb07a890-ce3c-55b2-bbd5-f52286f13740" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)\\right)$.\n\n{{derivative}}" :question/worked-solution "Work on the interior of the real domain: all real inputs, with $|x|>1$. For the inverse factor, the derivative formula gives $\\frac{d}{dx}\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Here the argument and its derivative are $u(x)=x$ and $u'(x)=1$.\n\nSet $p(x)=e^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)$. Then $p'(x)=e^{x}$ and $v'(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$. Apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=p'(x)v(x)+p(x)v'(x)\\\\\n&=\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)\\right)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\left(e^{x}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMove each unchanged factor into its fraction numerator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=e^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arcsec}(x)\\\\\n&\\quad +\\frac{e^{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Product Rule"}]}
